Context
The CMS requires secure authentication across web, mobile, and API channels. Tokens must carry tenant identity and user roles.

Decision
Use JSON Web Tokens (JWT) issued by an external Authentication Service (e.g., Azure AD / corporate IdP).

Rationale
Standardised, stateless authentication
Encodes tenant ID and user roles for RBAC checks
Supports SSO and MFA
Works well across micro front-ends and future services

Consequences
Token validation must occur on every request
Token expiry and refresh must be handled at gateway
Sensitive claims must never be trusted without signature verification

Alternatives Considered
Session-based auth → not suitable for distributed systems
API keys → no role or identity context
